{"id": "af2f06b3b54ee8224ce80e507f081c0b", "text": "can exert  control  on the minds  of even  learned  ones.  It is the nature  of sense  \norgans  to cause  turbulence  in one\u2019s  mind.  Hence,  one must  undertake  \ndifficult  rituals  such as fasting  on special  days etc., in addition  to spiritual  \nstudies  and try to overcome  the influence  of sense  organs  on one\u2019s mind.  \n \nThe sense organs  and the mind  are inert objects.  A question  then \narises  as to how these  inert objects  can exert  such control  over each other.", "embedding": [0.08748802542686462, -0.05852686986327171, -0.009534466080367565, 0.05445381626486778, -0.01093850377947092, -0.031549278646707535, 0.08696592599153519, -0.06008532643318176, 0.06729726493358612, 0.0061398958787322044, 0.06355848908424377, -0.021944215521216393, -0.02120932936668396, -0.03078542649745941, 0.020673595368862152, -0.019986266270279884, -0.019993266090750694, 0.0818917378783226, -0.10653167217969894, 0.08470223098993301, 0.006769087165594101, -0.011877568438649178, 0.0008476023213006556, 0.025210468098521233, -0.10508401691913605, 0.028923707082867622, -0.10462448745965958, -0.05897258222103119, 0.026811836287379265, -0.12153863906860352, 0.04541459307074547, -0.053548771888017654, -0.16468487679958344, 0.02680821157991886, -0.0638020932674408, 0.03704552352428436, 0.021370066329836845, 0.012250419706106186, 0.00028606512933038175, -0.0165056474506855, -0.03114107996225357, -0.028951432555913925, -0.02071942575275898, -0.05610569939017296, -0.011058703064918518, 0.09030736237764359, -0.025055142119526863, 0.03896867856383324, -0.03064422868192196, -0.05293703079223633, -0.18147939443588257, -0.01456495188176632, 0.03713543713092804, 0.02034209854900837, 0.021940933540463448, 0.045069094747304916, -0.0002804997784551233, 0.06984622776508331, -0.06282191723585129, -0.09392967820167542, 0.007453660946339369, -0.023044727742671967, 0.009000800549983978, -0.007750739809125662, -0.07596584409475327,